Pray when you are in 'big trouble' and have _no_other_means_to_survive_.
Big trouble is, e.g., being weak or fainting from food deficiency, or
being low at hit points (say 5 for less as a rule of thumb), when you
feel that you turn to stone, etc.

If you just pray to fix your food problem you may pray as often as you
become weak.  But if you pray a lot to fix different problems you have
to be attentive.

Don't pray when you've already prayed e.g. in the same combat. Try to
get some feeling about when it is ok to pray again.  A rule of thumb
(for me) is not before 1000 time steps passed - but I don't watch the
time counter for that purpose.  Don't pray when your god is displeased.

Sacrifice when your god is displeased on a co-aligned altar.  When you
want artifacts sacrifice corpses -  but watch your own needs for food.
Getting artifacts from your god might be a tenacious process.

